{"title":"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 21","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Spinners <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are spun. On each spinner, the arrow is equally likely to land on each number. What is the probability that the product of the two spinners' numbers is even?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/8/2b8c0e9de9eb3c68e3938fd3467803e6bbb24ef3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] pair A=(0,0); pair B=(3,0); draw(Circle(A,1)); draw(Circle(B,1));  draw((-1,0)--(1,0)); draw((0,1)--(0,-1)); draw((3,0)--(3,1)); draw((3+sqrt(3)/2,-.5)--(3,0)); draw((3,0)--(3-sqrt(3)/2,-.5));   label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(-1,1)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(2,1));  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(-.4,.4)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(.4,.4)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(.4,-.4)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;,(-.4,-.4)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(2.6,.4)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;,(3.4,.4)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;,(3,-.5));  [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"108\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/2/c0254b9c2a0eb922cc16bc7901aad6a1ee1a6a3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\frac14\\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ \\frac13\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ \\frac12\\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac23\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\frac34$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"367\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An even number comes from multiplying an even and even, even and odd, or odd and even. Since an odd number only comes from multiplying an odd and odd, there are less cases and it would be easier to find the probability of spinning two odd numbers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Multiply the independent probabilities of each spinner getting an odd number together and subtract it from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/d/bddedf7295c213c9be69119bbcc7eb0e4d721daa.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[1-\\frac24 \\cdot \\frac23 = 1- \\frac13 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac23}\\]\" width=\"221\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can make a chart and the we see that the 12 possibilities: 1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 6, 3, 6, 9, 4, 8, and 12. Out of these only 8 work; thus the probability is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/b/cbb27c511fa00a1566a341e0d8bd7569b33ceae0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac23}\\]\" width=\"60\" height=\"48\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We do a little bit of casework. In order to get a product that's even, we need at least one even number. First, we consider the probability of getting an even number on the first spinner, and then multiply by 1 because the second spinner can be anything. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/c/1dc39331ec2f5cb1aa9b0aff1a67cecb28f8cbdf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12 \\cdot 1 = \\frac12\\]\" width=\"69\" height=\"37\" />\nNext, we look at the chance that we don't get an even on the first spinner, but get an even on the second spinner (we don't do the probability of even on the second spinner multiplied by one because we would be double counting both spinners are even). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/0/5d005bf8b40b323f4394f0e52ea1b534dfc24178.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12 \\cdot \\frac13 = \\frac16\\]\" width=\"73\" height=\"37\" />\nAdd these two together to get the total probability, and we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/b/88b8b0c66335a515b0cc5360105135acdaa78165.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac12 + \\frac16 = \\frac46 = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ \\frac23}\\]\" width=\"167\" height=\"48\" />\n</p><p>~ligonmathkid2\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_21&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8\" title=\"2004 AMC 8\">2004 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2004\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2004 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\